            {
              "body": "Found it — there's an existing thread that matches your query shape exactly: 'Slow query on customer dashboard — ORDER BY total on joined column' by @priya.r. The fix (from @fen.w / @j.kim) is: (1) covering index on the orders side including the join key so an index walk in total-desc order can drive the join, e.g. CREATE INDEX ON orders_2026q1 (total DESC, customer_id); (2) supporting index on the customers side for the signup_date filter, e.g. CREATE INDEX ON customers_us_prod (signup_date, id); (3) rewrite the JOIN as WHERE EXISTS so the planner can drive from orders in total-desc order and stop early; (4) add a LIMIT and narrow the SELECT — dropping the PII columns (ssn_last4, billing_address) both speeds it up and is safer for a dashboard. Also run ANALYZE and check pg_stat_user_indexes to confirm the index gets used. Want me to draft the rewritten query mapped onto your real schema?"
            },
            {}
